      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "stellation of that name—a hundred physicians ) and is the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "crest-ornament of S'iva’s head, consumption does not leave",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "the Moon: or by whom can the ordinance of cruel Fate be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "transgressed ?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "97. That, which is fixed as a man’s portion in this world",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "by all-powerful Destiny, will go to him; patronage of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "great ( lit. great patronage ) is not at all the cause ( of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "aquisition ). Although the cloud, the gratifier of the desires",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "of all beings, showers daily, only two or three minute drops",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "of water fall into the mouth of the châtaka.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "98. When on the branch of the karira tree there is not a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "single leaf, it is not the fault of the spring. If the owl cannot",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "see by day what blame is due to the sun ? Showers of rain",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "do not fall into the mouth of the châtaka; but why blame",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "the cloud for that ? Who is able to wipe off what has",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "once been written on the forehead by fate ?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "99. We shall bow to the gods, but then, even they are",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "subject to the accursed fate; (in that case) fate ought to re-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "ceive our homage; but even fate dispenses but the fruits con-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "sistent with each action. The fruit being dependent on action,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "what (have we to do) with the gods and what with fate ! Bow",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "to those Karmans then, which even fate cannot control.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "100. A bow to that Karman by whom Brahmâ was",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "confined in the interior of the pot-like primordial egg ( there",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "to evolve his creation) like a potter; by whom Vishnu was",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "hurled into the very troublesome intricacy of the ten incar-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "nations; by whom S'iva has been compelled to wander for",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "alms skull in hand; and in obedience to whom the sun ever",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "roams in the sky.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "101. A handsome form avails not; neither does descent",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "nor character; not even learning, nor service assiduously",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
